.TH PMASKD 8 "2026" "pmaskd 0.2.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
pmaskd \- run masked jobs for local clients that do not hold the secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmaskd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmaskd
holds a job environment in memory, redacts its own
.B /proc
entry, and executes masked jobs for local clients.
Each client sends a command and receives the job's standard I/O and exit status.
The client never holds the job environment.
.PP
.B Warning:
An allowed uid can execute arbitrary programs with the daemon's privileges and inherit its environment.
Grant
.B \-\-allow\-uid
only to uids already trusted with that access.
On a root daemon, pass
.B \-\-run\-as\-uid
to run each job under the client's uid and gid.
.PP
.B pmaskd
does not open the encrypted secret store.
Run
.B "pmask agent"
to unlock and serve the store, and deliver secrets with
.B "\-\-secret NAME=agent:NAME" .
.B pmaskd
rejects
.B \-\-store
and
.B \-\-passphrase\-file
as unknown options with exit 255.
Load job environments only with
.BR \-\-env\-file .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Set the Unix socket path to bind.
Default:
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR /pmask.sock
when owned by the effective uid and not group-writable or world-writable, or
.B /run/pmask.sock
as root.
Otherwise
.B \-\-socket
is required.
.B pmaskd
never falls back to
.B /tmp
because a world-writable directory cannot verify ownership safely.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-label " \fINAME\fR"
Set the default presentation label when a client sends none.
Default:
.BR pmask\-job .
A client
.B \-\-label
replaces it, and
.B \-\-label\-empty
sets an empty label.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-env\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Load
.B KEY=VALUE
lines into the job environment.
Repeat this option to layer multiple files.
Later files override earlier files.
The parser skips blank lines and # comments and allows an optional
.B export
prefix.
KEY must contain printable ASCII without spaces or =.
The parser trims surrounding blanks from VALUE, removes one matching pair of single or double quotes, and rejects NUL bytes.
No escape sequences apply.
Parse errors name the file and line number.
.B pmaskd
warns when FILE is readable by group or others.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-inherit\-env
Pass only
.B \-\-env\-file
variables to jobs instead of inheriting the daemon environment.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-env
Leave
.B /proc/\fIpid\fB/environ
visible for jobs.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow\-uid " UID"
Accept connections from UID in addition to the daemon's own uid and root.
Repeat this option to allow multiple uids.
.TP
.B \-\-run\-as\-uid
Run each job with the connecting client's uid and gid.
Requires a root daemon.
Combine with a reachable socket mode such as
.B "\-\-socket\-mode 666"
when serving other uids.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket\-mode " OCT"
Set socket permission bits in octal.
Default: 600.
.TP
.BI \-\-io\-timeout " SECONDS"
Drop a client that stalls while sending its request or reading its response.
Default: 30.
Pass 0 for no limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-job\-timeout " SECONDS"
Kill a job tree after SECONDS and return exit code 137.
Default: no limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Run up to N concurrent jobs, spawning one worker process per connection.
Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-job\-bytes " N"
Set the maximum total byte size of job arguments, counting each trailing NUL byte.
Default: 1048576.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log each accepted job.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help text.
.SH PROTOCOL
Each connection carries one request and one job.
.PP
Client to daemon, with
.B SCM_RIGHTS
carrying exactly three descriptors (stdin, stdout, stderr):
.PP
.RS
1 byte version (2)
.br
"PMK2"  u8 label_mode  u32 label_len  label
.br
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ u32 argc
.br
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ argc * (u32 len, bytes)
.RE
.PP
.I label_mode
is 0 for the daemon label, 1 for an empty label, and 2 for the attached label text.
.PP
A
.B PING
request sends the four bytes
.B PMKP
with no body.
.B pmaskd
runs the same uid check as a job request and replies with
.B key=value
lines.
The daemon's own uid and root receive full policy fields, including allowed uids, socket mode, timeouts, argument cap, and peer-identity method.
Another uid admitted by
.B \-\-allow\-uid
receives only protocol version,
.BR detail=reduced ,
label, daemon uid, and
.BR run_as_uid .
Refused uids receive only the refusal line.
The reply never includes environment variable values.
.PP
Daemon to client:
.PP
.RS
i32 exit_code  u32 has_signal  i32 signal  u32 msg_len  msg
.RE
.PP
All integers use little-endian byte order.
Limits:
.B argc
<= 4096, one argument <= 1 MiB, full request <= 8 MiB, label <= 4096 bytes.
.SH AUTHORISATION
.B SO_PEERCRED
controls access.
.B pmaskd
accepts its own uid and root by default and pins each accepted peer via
.B SO_PEERPIDFD
or
.B /proc
start time, failing closed if neither succeeds.
The socket defaults to mode 0600, configurable with
.BR \-\-socket\-mode .
The client also verifies the daemon's peer uid before sending a request.
.SH SOCKET SAFETY
.B pmaskd
refuses to start if the socket path is a symlink, a non-socket file, or an active daemon socket.
Before binding,
.B pmaskd
opens the parent directory with
.B O_NOFOLLOW
and verifies ownership by the effective uid with no group or world write bits.
Any directory
.B pmaskd
creates uses mode 0700.
.B pmaskd
binds under umask 077, applies the socket mode, and verifies that the bound socket matches the created node.
.SH EXIT STATUS AND REFUSALS
.B pmaskd
serves until
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT .
On shutdown,
.B pmaskd
kills active jobs, zeroes its stored environment, removes the socket, and exits 0.
Startup failures print one line prefixed with
.B "pmaskd: "
and exit 255.
Refused clients print the daemon's line and exit 255.
.TP
.B "unknown option"
Rejects unsupported options, including
.B \-\-store
and
.BR \-\-passphrase\-file .
Exit 255.
.TP
.B "socket directory"
Parent directory is not owned by the effective uid or is group-writable or world-writable.
.B pmaskd
prints path, mode, and reason and exits 255.
.TP
.B "socket path"
Path is a symlink, a non-socket file, or an active socket.
Exit 255.
.TP
.B "protocol version"
Client sends a version other than 2.
.B pmaskd
returns its version and keeps serving.
The client exits 255.
.TP
.B "uid is not allowed"
Peer uid is not the daemon uid, root, or an
.B \-\-allow\-uid
entry.
.B pmaskd
refuses the connection and the client exits 255.
.TP
.B "\-\-jobs and \-\-max\-job\-bytes"
Values below 1 exit 255.
.TP
.B "\-\-run\-as\-uid"
Non-root daemons refuse this flag and exit 255.
.TP
.B "job timeout"
Jobs exceeding
.B \-\-job\-timeout
are killed and return status 137.
.PP
Job exit statuses, including signal deaths, pass through to the client untouched.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmask (1)
